package VirtualFCS "VirtualFCS-SysVal - PEM fuel cell system model based on VirtualFCS"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Package;
  // import Annex60;
  annotation(
    preferredView="info",
    version="2.1.0-dev",
    versionDate="2023-01-19",
    uses(Modelica(version = "4.0.0"), Buildings(version = "10.0.0")),
    Icon(graphics = {Rectangle(fillColor = {255, 255, 255}, fillPattern = FillPattern.Solid, extent = {{-100, 100}, {100, -100}}), Bitmap(origin = {-1, 0}, extent = {{-99, -100}, {99, 100}}, fileName = "modelica://VirtualFCS/Resources/images/virtual-fcs-logo-emblem.png")}),
    Documentation(info = "<html><head></head><body><p><b>Overview</b></p><p>VirtualFCS is a Modelica library for dynamic system simulation of proton exchange membrane fuel cell (PEMFC) systems. It contains:</p><ul><li><a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.Electrochemical\">Electrochemical</a>: PEM fuel cell stack, algebraic cell-voltage model and fuel cell system.</li><li><a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.SubSystems\">SubSystems</a>: hydrogen supply with anode recirculation, air supply (compressor or mass-flow controlled) and cooling loop variants.</li><li><a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.Fluid\">Fluid</a> and <a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.Thermal\">Thermal</a>: balance-of-plant components (membrane humidifier, map-based compressor and recirculation blower, coolant pump, flow resistances, valve characteristics, heat exchanger).</li><li><a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.Utilities\">Utilities</a>: operating-point input (SystemControl), polynomial maps and helper functions.</li><li><a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.ComponentTesting\">ComponentTesting</a>: test models; TestFuelCellSystem is the reference system simulation.</li></ul><p>The library version is given by the <code>version</code> annotation of this package. Dependencies: Modelica Standard Library 4.0.0 and Buildings 10.0.0 (see the <code>uses</code> annotation).</p><p><b>Operating-point input (OpCons)</b></p><p>Operating points are supplied as a Modelica text table named <code>op_cons</code> (<code>float op_cons(nrows, ncols)</code>, first column = time [s]). By default the file <code>modelica://VirtualFCS/Resources/LuT/OpCons_data.txt</code> is used. This file is an interface: external software overwrites it, so its content and column layout change with the use case. The column layout must match the structure of the simulated model. A model can instead reference a dedicated file with the same table format via <code>fileName</code>. See <a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.Utilities.SystemControl\">SystemControl</a>.</p><p><b>VirtualFCS-SysVal</b></p><p>This version, VirtualFCS-SysVal 2.1.0-sysval, is based on the development state 2.1.0-dev of VirtualFCS after its release v2.0.0 (MIT license, Copyright (c) 2021 Virtual-FCS H2020) and is extended for the PEM fuel cell system of the accompanying publication. It is not an official VirtualFCS release. It contains the parameter set of the second iteration of the validation process. The published model uses the default membrane parameters of Hahn (2023).</p><p><b>Author</b></p><p>Luis M. Winkler (Zentrum f&uuml;r Sonnenenergie- und Wasserstoff-Forschung Baden-W&uuml;rttemberg (ZSW), Ulm, Germany, Chair of Electrical Energy Systems (EES), University of Bayreuth, Germany, and Institute for Sustainable Energy Systems (ISES), Munich University of Applied Sciences, Germany)</p><p><b>Funding</b></p><p>This work was supported in part by the Federal Ministry for Economic Affairs and Climate Action (BMWK) within the project AVICELL (grant number 20M1903C).</p><p><b>Upstream VirtualFCS</b></p><p>VirtualFCS was developed in the project Virtual-FCS, which received funding from the European Union&#39;s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under grant agreement No 875087. Its contributors are listed in <a href=\"modelica://VirtualFCS.UsersGuide.Acknowledgements\">Acknowledgements</a>.</p></body></html>"));
end VirtualFCS;
